Day 42: Walk in the Light | Tuesday of Holy Week (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Walk while you have the light.”
Not later.
Not eventually.
Now.

Welcome to Day 42 of our Lent journey, deep within the heart of Holy Week.
Today’s reflection invites you to step into the light of Christ — a light that does not shame, but frees; a light that does not expose to wound, but to heal; a light that brings clarity, courage, and truth.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that walking in the light is not about perfection. It is about direction — choosing honesty over hiding, courage over fear, integrity over convenience. Jesus shines His light not to condemn you, but to liberate you.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Jesus calls you to walk in the light with courage and honesty

How His light brings healing, clarity, and freedom

Why Holy Week invites you to step out of the shadows

A prayer to walk in God’s truth with integrity

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, let me walk in Your light.”

